{
  "headline": "Awutu Senya West MP expresses confidence in NDC retaining parliamentary seat",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Gizela Tetteh-Agbotui, the Member of Parliament for Awutu Senya West in Ghana, stated she is confident the National Democratic Congress (NDC) will retain the constituency in the next general election. Her comments were made during the NDC constituency executive elections, where she dismissed concerns that the recent election of a New Patriotic Party (NPP) regional chairman from the area might improve the NPP's chances of winning the parliamentary seat. Dr. Kwabena Essibu, who is from Senya Breku within the constituency, was recently elected as the Central Regional chairman of the NPP. Tetteh-Agbotui disclosed that she personally congratulated Dr. Essibu on his election but informed him of her determination to retain the seat for the NDC. She described the constituency as an important electoral hold for her party and urged NDC members to maintain unity following the constituency executive elections. Tetteh-Agbotui called on the newly elected executives to strengthen party structures and mobilize members ahead of the next general election."
    }
  ]
}

